  "question": {
    "text": "A train of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>150</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> length is going towards north direction at a speed of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. A parrot flies at a speed of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> towards south direction parallel to the railway track. The time taken by the parrot to cross the train is equal to"
